    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394-a1">

                <pb facs="0929" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg833"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No.
                    1017.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">mines in sonora</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Monitor Republicano, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1879-08-06">August 6,
                        1879</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The government of the State has issued a circular to the prefects of the
                    districts which in its essential part says:</p>
                <p>“It being ordained by the general law of the 1st of February, 1856, that
                    foreigners cannot acquire in the frontier States or territories of the nation
                    real estate, including mines, within a zone of twenty leagues from the dividing
                    line, unless by the previous <pb facs="0930" n="834" xml:id="pg834"/> permission
                    of the President of the republic, the governor of the State of Sonora ordered
                    the prefects to have very special care that in the registers or pre-emptions
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">denuncios</hi>) of mines forwarded to the
                    government through the prefectures, and in which one or more foreigners are
                    interested, they always state the distance from the dividing line of the United
                    States of the North the mine referred to in the document is located, to the end
                    that the executive may the more easily decide which can or cannot be admitted in
                    view of the prohibition referred to.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
